# Release signing — copy to `android/key.properties` and fill in.
#
# ⛔ NEVER COMMIT THE REAL FILE OR THE KEYSTORE. `.gitignore` already excludes
# both; this example exists so the four names are documented somewhere public
# without any value being.
#
# The signing key IS the update channel: Android refuses an update whose
# signature does not match the installed app, so this key must not change once
# anybody has installed a release built with it. Losing it means every user has
# to uninstall and reinstall, which takes their keystore — strap pairing, session,
# device token — with it. Back it up somewhere you would trust with a password
# manager's own export.
#
# Create one with:
#   keytool -genkey -v -keystore ~/healthee-release.jks -storetype JKS \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000 -alias healthee
#
# CI reads the same four values from the environment instead:
#   HEALTHEE_KEYSTORE_PATH · HEALTHEE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
#   HEALTHEE_KEY_ALIAS     · HEALTHEE_KEY_PASSWORD

storeFile=/absolute/path/to/healthee-release.jks
storePassword=
keyAlias=healthee
keyPassword=
